{
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||Part 1 -1 The boy's name was Santiago.": "第1部分-1男孩的名字是聖地牙哥。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||Dusk was falling as the boy arrived with his herd at an abandoned church.": "當男孩帶著牛羣來到一座廢棄的教堂時，黃昏正在墜落。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||The roof had fallen in long ago, and an enormous sycamore had grown on the spot where the sacristy had once stood.": "屋頂很久以前就倒塌了，一個巨大的梧桐樹生長在聖器室曾經站立的地方。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||He decided to spend the night there.": "他決定在那裡過夜",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||He saw to it that all the sheep entered through the ruined gate, and then laid some planks across it to prevent the flock from wandering away during the night.": "他確保所有的羊都從毀壞的門進入，然後在門上放一些木板，以防止羊羣在夜間徘徊。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||There were no wolves in the region, but once an animal had strayed during the night, and the boy had had to spend the entire next day searching for it.": "該地區沒有狼，但一旦一隻動物在夜間迷路，男孩就不得不花整整一天的時間尋找它。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||He swept the floor with his jacket and lay down, using the book he had just finished reading as a pillow.": "他用外套掃地，用剛讀完的書當枕頭躺下。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||He told himself that he would have to start reading thicker books.": "他告訴自己，他必須開始讀更厚的書。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||They lasted longer and made more comfortable pillows.": "使用壽命更長，枕頭更舒適。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||It was still dark when he awoke and looking up he could see the stars through the half -destroyed roof.": "當他醒來時，天還很黑，擡頭一看，他可以看到半個被毀壞的屋頂上的星星。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||I wanted to sleep a little longer, he thought.": "我想再睡一會，他想。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||He had had the same dream that night as a week ago, and once again he had awakened before it ended.": "那天晚上，他和一個星期前做了同樣的夢，在夢結束之前，他又一次醒來。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||He arose and, taking up his crook, began to awaken the sheep that still slept.": "他站起來，抱起他的騙子，開始喚醒還在睡覺的羊。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||He had noticed that as soon as he awoke most of his animals also began to stir.": "他注意到，當他醒來時，他的大多數動物也開始攪拌。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||It was as if some mysterious energy bound his life to that of the sheep, with whom he had spent the past two years, leading them through the countryside in search of food and water.": "彷彿某種神祕的能量將他的生命與過去兩年與他一起度過的綿羊的生命結合在一起，帶領他們穿越鄉村尋找食物和水。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||They are so used to me that they know my schedule, he muttered.": "他們太習慣我了，他們知道我的日程安排，他喃喃自語。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||Thinking about that for a moment he realized that it could be the other way around, that it was he who had become accustomed to their schedule.": "想了一會兒，他意識到這可能是另一回事，是他已經習慣了他們的日程安排。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||But there were certain of them who took a bit longer to awaken.": "但有些人花了更長的時間才醒來。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||The boy prodded them one by one with his crook calling each by name.": "那個男孩一個接一個地戳他們，他的騙子叫著每個人的名字。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||He had always believed that the sheep were able to understand what he said.": "他一直相信羊能理解他所說的話。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||So there were times when he read them parts of his books that had made an impression on him, or when he would tell them of the loneliness or the happiness of a shepherd in the fields.": "因此，有時候他會讀一些讓他印象深刻的書，或者告訴他們田野牧羊人的寂寞或幸福。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||Sometimes he would comment to them on the things he had seen in the villages they passed.": "有時候，他會向他們評論在他們經過的村莊中看到的事情。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||But for the past few days he had spoken to them about only one thing—the girl, the daughter of a merchant who lived in the village they would reach in about four days.": "但在過去的幾天裡，他只跟他們談了一件事，那就是女孩，一個住在村子裡的商人的女兒，他們大約四天後就會到達。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||He had been to the village only once, the year before.": "一年前，他只去過村子一次。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||The merchant was the proprietor of a dry goods shop, and he always demanded that the sheep be sheared in his presence so that he would not be cheated.": "商人是一家乾貨店的老闆，他一直要求在他面前剪羊毛，以免被欺騙。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||A friend had told the boy about the shop and he had taken his sheep there.": "一個朋友告訴了那個男孩關於商店的事，他把他的羊帶到了那裡。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||I need to sell some wool, the boy told the merchant.": "男孩告訴商人，我需要賣一些羊毛。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||The shop was busy and the man asked the shepherd to wait until the afternoon.": "商店很忙，那人叫牧羊人等到下午。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||So the boy sat on the steps of the shop and took a book from his bag.": "於是男孩坐在商店的臺階上，從包裡拿出一本書。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||I didn't know shepherds knew how to read, said a girl's voice behind him.": "我不知道牧羊人會讀書，身後有個女孩的聲音說。",
  "The Alchemist of Part 1-01 Timestamp.txt||The girl was typical of the region of Andalusia, with flowing black hair and eyes that vaguely recalled the Moorish conquerors.": "這個女孩是典型的安達盧西亞地區，黑色的頭髮和眼睛流動，模糊地回憶起摩爾人的徵服者。"
}